the same for the same system, and `johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_reps` the statement in Mathlib's terms alone (`IsPolyRootEq`):
`ν Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron` is the first coordinate of the root of each of these systems, each with exactly one root in its
box; it implies `IsPolyRootMax` (`IsPolyRootEq.isPolyRootMax`). There is one system (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootMax.isRootEq_singleton`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonBilunabirotunda`, `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonBilunabirotunda.Exact` and
`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonBilunabirotunda.Roots`, which it does not change.
-/

namespace Nieuwland.Polyhedra

set_option maxHeartbeats 0 in
/-- **Every system of `ν Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron` has its one root at `ν Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron`**: each of the systems of `johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_roots_list` has exactly one root, and its scale is the Nieuwland number. -/
theorem johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_shared_list :
    PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_system_0] Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron.nieuwland :=
  PolynomialSystem.IsRootMax.isRootEq_singleton johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_roots_list

/-- **The representatives of `ν Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron`**: the same system, each with exactly one root, at the scale `ν Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron`. -/
theorem johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_reps_list :
    PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_system_0] Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron.nieuwland :=
  johnsonBilunabirotunda_nu_shared_list

